  "id": "Compound::DB01288 - Gene::154",
  "verbalization": "Fenoterol, a selective beta-2 adrenergic receptor agonist, is shown to bind to Adrb3 and participate in Beta-adrenergic Receptor Activity, which is linked to Adrb2. This suggests a potential mechanism where Fenoterol may influence Adrb2 through the activation of Adrb3. The evidence from multiple paths indicates that Fenoterol interacts with Adrb3, which in turn is involved in the activity of Adrb2, suggesting a possible role in modulating Adrb2 function. The consistent binding to Adrb3 across different paths supports a direct interaction, while the participation in Beta-adrenergic Receptor Activity implies a broader signaling pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Fenoterol could influence Adrb2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Fenoterol and Adrb2, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise role of Adrb3 in this relationship.",
